": {\n    \"message\": \"deft-blanket-clover-43\"\n  }\n}\n== web-administratively-speaking/\n{\n  \"77be6d06-e15f-458a-a0aa-a9f5741c2720\": {\n    \"proof-1\": \"proof_cdb74758565d459cb55fcd1373391c1a\"\n  }\n}\n== web-stay-in-your-directory/\n{\n  \"af02a536-b90b-49b9-a409-4e710f8b180a\": {\n    \"proof-1\": \"proof_0ccb83154638461b8b6626ac64977cc7\"\n  }\n}\n\n## Proposed lib additions\n- `lib.common.fast_aes_unzip(data, passwords)` -> [(name, Future[bytes])] + sha256 cache: the `_aes_member` / `_fast_unzip` pair in day09 binary-nimble solve.py (WinZip AE-x without pyzipper's pure-Python HMAC pass; zlib/pycryptodome/hashlib release the GIL so members inflate in parallel). Every lane whose evidence.zip carries a large member benefits.\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no answer change) the \"8.21s on single_solve\" flag was CPU contention from parallel solver-tests, not the solver: isolated it runs 0.55-0.60 s wall on the single (taskset 2 vCPUs, ~0.75 s CPU) and 1.2 s on a 3-set Mastery; critical path is the d08 67 MB Swift member's AES-CTR||inflate||sha256 pipeline (done at ~0.37 s) + ~0.09 s of field analysis -- measure with `taskset -c 0,1 /usr/bin/time python3 solve.py ...`, not under a loaded solver-test.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D14) the \"4.11 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~4.5) -- isolated and pinned to 2 CPUs: single 0.51 s wall (0.6 s unpinned; the harness cProfile itself shows 0.048 s for import), 5-set Mastery auto-mastery-7439276e 1.42 s wall pinned / 0.80 s unpinned; all 21 cases pass with every answer_id filled. Nothing to trim that the earlier cycles have not already trimmed.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D15) the \"4.84 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~6.6, harness cProfile counted 1.1 s of imports and 2.9 s of thread waits) -- isolated and pinned to 2 CPUs: single 0.90 s wall (critical path = AES-CTR+inflate of the 67 MB d08 member ~0.2 s, HCFG scans 0.09 s, capstone import 0.07 s), 5-set Mastery auto-mastery-546ae191 2.6 s pinned / 1.4 s unpinned; all 23 cases pass with every answer_id filled (solver-test single 1.26 s under concurrent load).\n\n## D17 (decoder-ring) single\n- New re-asked earlier-day fields (all GM-accepted): d01 marker (.huntress string), recover_code (imm of recover_code), d02\n  mangled_score_symbol (_ZNK15DiscoveryEngine5scoreEPKc), typeinfo_symbol (_ZTI of the score class), d04 has_go_runtime,\n  d05 has_rust_mangled_symbol, d06 methods (Main-Class method-table names incl. <init>) / access_flags (class access_flags\n  decimal, 49), d07 method_count (incl. <init>/<clinit>, 7) / has_coroutine_runtime (kotlin/coroutines/ entries -> true).\n- hcfg_storage: `base64` GM-confirmed for base64-stored blobs (d08/09/11/13). RAW-stored (d12 FPC .data, d14 .hcfg section):\n  label UNRESOLVED -- `raw`, `section`, `.hcfg`-family combos, byte/array/binary/xor/blob rejected; see single_solve/HELP.md.\n\n## Proposed lib additions\n- lib/vocab.json: storage / hcfg_storage = \"base64\" for a base64 (SENGR...) stored HCFG (GM D17 d09/d08/d11/d13); \"raw\" REJECTED for raw-stored (D17 d12/d14).\n\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D17) the \"3.31 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~4.5; harness cProfile counted ~1.1 s of imports and ~2.4 s of thread waits) -- isolated: solve.py 0.8-0.9 s wall on the 204-id single (run_solver 0.87 s; tottime is 0.24 s threaded zlib inflate of the AES members + ~0.2 s imports), 1.1 s inside the full concurrent solver-test; all 31 cases green. `hctf solver-run` wall (~6.5 s) is CLI/harness startup under load, not the solver. d12/d14 `hcfg_storage` (raw-stored) stay intentionally empty (unresolved GM label), so the single outputs 202/204.\n\n## Proposed lib additions\n- lib/meta/prebuilt/macho.py: field `cpu_type_set` = JSON list of cputype \"0x%08x\" per slice (fat_arch order, thin = header); GM-confirmed D20 thin arm64 -> [\"0x0100000c\"] (fat order/dedupe unverified)\n# Day 7 — Node by Node (script-analysis, node operation graphs)\n\nConcept: one evidence.zip with 61 members (PowerShell samples, JScript/Batch/VBScript/Python/Bash/Node operation\ngraphs); each graph decodes to a plan (steps/adapter/campaign/indicator) and is sorted into a role.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none in the bytes. TT attempt 26b7da83 failed because its download was the GM body `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` (24 B saved as evidence.zip, sha != contract sha256), so every field came out None/default. The harvested variants 49b73141 + 7d6f8d53 were already answered 469/469 by the current solver (spot-checked against the raw bytes; their expected.json is solver-derived, not GM-verified). Parse rule: if every artifact is a small `{\"error\": ...}` JSON, exit non-zero (solve.py now does) instead of guessing roles. The bytes-less case was removed from cases/ (still kept under time_trial/attempts/26b7da83).\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none (Day 8 TT). The start returned 503 `training_rotation_invalid` with no attempt and no artifact, so there were no variant bytes. The solver answers the TT contract's 615 ids 615/615 on the single's bytes. Rule: a start error is an orchestrator retry, not a solver change.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none in the bytes (D8 Mastery 7432c509). Same 5-set bundle shape (outer zip holding evidence-01..05.zip) as the GM-verified auto-mastery cases; the solver answered 3075/3075 but the attempt EXPIRED (submit RemoteDisconnected after 5.42 s solve on Homebase). expected.json = solver output, spot-checked against the raw bytes (PS base64 record, VBS Codec_ field, While/if-errorlevel control). Speed fix: sets solve in forked processes (group_by_set + ProcessPoolExecutor, sequential fallback); the nested-zip index no longer decrypts every script leaf just to sniff for PK (375 PBKDF2s -> only the members asked, per set, in parallel); powerplay.xor is one big-int XOR.\n\n## Proposed lib additions\n- `lib.common.gm_error_body(artdir) -> bytes|None`: detect a GM error JSON (`rate_limited`, ...) saved in place of an\n  artifact, so every solver fails loudly. Better still: the harness download step (hctf/hb_timed.py) should retry on\n  `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` and never save it as the artifact. That would have saved this timed attempt.\n- `lib.common.iter_entries(root, leaf_ext=...)`: don't load a member just to sniff for a nested zip when its name has a script/text extension (.js/.ps1/.py/.vbs/.cmd/.bat/.sh/.mjs/.php/...). Today it decrypts every AES member of a Mastery bundle up front (375 PBKDF2 = ~0.2 s locally, many times that on Homebase), and each forked set repeats it. See `_iter_entries` in this solve.py.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4f2bef86-ad73-4ea2-9b45-3318d4f5063d","uuid":"53bc0661-3289-4d1d-825a-63caa0871321","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:15:19.139Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"== binary-resourceful/\n{\n  \"938afd7e-46c4-473c-85ed-878290b3d960\": {\n    \"d01_artifact_sha256_1\": \"a0d3aeddb90dccf579e0262704dc7d7c2828121d8cc988f085de169601737b9b\",\n    \"d01_analysis_elf_class\": \"ELF64\",\n    \"d01_analysis_machine\": \"x86-64\",\n    \"d01_analysis_section_names\": \"[\\\"\\\",\\\".interp\\\",\\\".note.gnu.property\\\",\\\".note.ABI-tag\\\",\\\".hash\\\",\\\".gnu.hash\\\",\\\".dynsym\\\",\\\".dynstr\\\",\\\".gnu.version\\\",\\\".gnu.version_r\\\",\\\".rela.dyn\\\",\\\".init\\\",\\\".text\\\",\\\".fini\\\",\\\".rodata\\\",\\\".huntress\\\",\\\".eh_frame_hdr\\\",\\\".eh_frame\\\",\\\".init_array\\\",\\\".fini_array\\\",\\\".dynamic\\\",\\\".got\\\",\\\".got.plt\\\",\\\".data\\\",\\\".bss\\\",\\\".symtab\\\",\\\".strtab\\\",\\\".shstrtab\\\"]\",\n    \"d01_analysis_symbols\": \"[\\\"crt1.o\\\",\\\"__abi_tag\\\",\\\"variant-000.c\\\",\\\"marker\\\",\\\"crtstuff.c\\\",\\\"deregister_tm_clones\\\",\\\"register_tm_clones\\\",\\\"__do_global_dtors_aux\\\",\\\"completed.0\\\",\\\"__do_global_dtors_aux_fini_array_entry\\\",\\\"frame_dummy\\\",\\\"__frame_dummy_init_array_ent