{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDZVaQKspHv2TzKGVHRB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The day20 ratchet gate is green (`python3 -m hctf.orchestrate ratchet-gate day20`, exit 0). The first run failed on one of my own new test lines, which expected a Python list where `meta.answer` returns compact JSON. I fixed that line; no existing assertion was touched.\n\n1. **Metadata (the one proposal, merged):** `macho.cpu_type_set` now lives in a new `lib/meta/macho.py` and is registered as verified for day 20 in `lib/meta/__init__.py`. The GM accepted `[\"0x0100000c\"]` on the Single, the Time Trial and all 5 Mastery sets, and rejected `[\"arm64\"]`. I recorded both in `lib/knowledge.py` (`MACHO_CPU_TYPE_SET` and `_REJECTED`). Every variant was a thin (single-architecture) binary, so slice order for universal binaries is still untested.\n2. **Warmups (not proposed, merged):** added the day 20 codec to `lib/warmups_codecs.py`: hex of the `feff` byte-order mark plus UTF-16 big-endian text. Re-encoding gives the exact original bytes on the Single, the Time Trial and all 98 Mastery line-20 chunks. `decode_chunked` already decodes it and returned all 98 Mastery slugs correctly.\n3. **Binary (not proposed, merged):** added `lib.binary.resource_overlay` and an RS20 branch in `overlay_unpack`. The existing RS20 handling assumed the day 19 layout and returned nothing on day 20 files. The new branch checks the exact end-of-file bound and the scratch SHA-256, and matches the GM's config and resource size (380) on all 7 day 20 binaries.\n4. **No lib change for the other lanes:** mobile is already answered by the existing `lib.android` string scans. The script lane solved its Jenkins/Groovy specimens with the existing `lib.codec`, and its solver has no day 20 code. The web lane (including the Mastery case that needed a fix) only changed its own solver's path-traversal probing, and there is no web module in lib to add it to.\n5. **Tests:** one check each for the warmups codec, the Mach-O field and the RS20 overlay, added to `tests/test_day7_fixes.py`. Separately, the warmups Mastery solve took 18.6 s, but the lib decoder handles the whole bundle in 0.07 s, so the time is going somewhere else."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":689,"cache_read_input_tokens":111481,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":689},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4f2bef86-ad73-4ea2-9b45-3318d4f5063d","uuid":"bad7f19c-f8fb-4666-9a6a-9336c7d2cec9","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:23:18.210Z","request_id":"req_011CgDZVZjeRP54pj4QVzV1Q"}
